@page "/privacy"
@layout MarketingLayout

<PageTitle>Privacy Policy | My Active Vitals</PageTitle>

<article class="legal-page">
    <p class="marketing-kicker">Legal</p>
    <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
    <p class="legal-updated">Draft for development review · Last updated July 16, 2026</p>

    <p>This policy describes how My Active Vitals collects, uses, and protects information when you use our website and personal health tracking application.</p>

    <section>
        <h2>Information you provide</h2>
        <p>We may collect account information such as your name, email address, password credentials in protected form, profile preferences, and the health and wellness information you choose to enter. This can include nutrition, exercise, blood pressure, glucose, weight, fluid intake, medication-related notes, and laboratory information.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Information collected automatically</h2>
        <p>We may collect technical information needed to operate and secure the service, such as IP address, browser type, device information, request logs, authentication events, and diagnostic data.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>How information is used</h2>
        <ul>
            <li>Provide, maintain, secure, and improve My Active Vitals</li>
            <li>Authenticate accounts and preserve user preferences</li>
            <li>Generate the summaries, estimates, and trends you request</li>
            <li>Respond to support requests and service communications</li>
            <li>Detect misuse, investigate errors, and meet legal obligations</li>
        </ul>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>AI-assisted features</h2>
        <p>When you request an AI-assisted nutrition estimate, the food description and relevant request details may be sent to an AI service provider to generate the result. Avoid entering names or unrelated sensitive information in food descriptions. AI estimates may be incomplete or inaccurate and should be reviewed before use.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Service providers</h2>
        <p>We may use service providers for hosting, databases, security, email, customer support, analytics, AI processing, and payment processing. They receive only the information needed to perform services for us and are subject to their own contractual and security obligations.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Payments</h2>
        <p>When subscriptions launch, payment information will be collected and processed by our payment provider. My Active Vitals will not directly store full payment card numbers.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Retention and deletion</h2>
        <p>We retain information while your account is active and as reasonably necessary to provide the service, resolve disputes, maintain security, and comply with law. Account deletion and data export procedures will be described before paid subscriptions launch.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Security</h2>
        <p>We use administrative and technical safeguards intended to protect information. No internet service can guarantee absolute security, and you are responsible for protecting your account credentials and devices.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Your choices</h2>
        <p>You may review and update profile information through your account. You may also contact us about access, correction, export, or deletion requests. Rights vary depending on where you live.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Children</h2>
        <p>My Active Vitals is intended for adults and is not directed to children under 18. We do not knowingly collect personal information directly from children.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Policy changes</h2>
        <p>We may update this policy as the service changes. We will post the revised date and provide additional notice when required.</p>
    </section>

    <section>
        <h2>Contact</h2>
        <p>Questions about this policy can be sent to <a href="mailto:support@myactivevitals.com">support@myactivevitals.com</a>.</p>
    </section>
</article>
